<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 8.808 percent on Thursday from 9.049 percent at the previous auction on May 15.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 1.1 billion pounds and accepted bids for 1,410.425 million. Bills worth 980.775 million pounds mature today.</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: August 21, 1997 (August 14, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.808 percent (9.049)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,410.425 million (1,003.05 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 2,690.45 million (1,921.05 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.499-8.838 percent (8.876-9.049)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.499-9.888 percent (9.876-9.720)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 91  (127)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 219 (315)</p>
<p>($1 = 3.395 Egyptian pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
